## Scenarios

### game2d.render.evidence — find_centroid

#### single marked pixel in a 4x4 buffer returns its exact coordinates

- Verify: single marked pixel in a 4x4 buffer returns its exact coordinates


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 10 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: single marked pixel in a 4x4 buffer returns its exact coordinates")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val bg: u32 = 0xFF000000
val mark: u32 = 0xFFFF0000
var px: [u32] = [bg; 16]
px[1 * 4 + 2] = mark
val c = find_centroid(px, 4, 4, mark)
assert_equal(c[0], 2)
assert_equal(c[1], 1)
assert_equal(c[2], 1)
```

</details>

#### two marked pixels average to the exact integer centroid

- Verify: two marked pixels average to the exact integer centroid


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: two marked pixels average to the exact integer centroid")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val bg: u32 = 0xFF000000
val mark: u32 = 0xFF00FF00
var px: [u32] = [bg; 16]
px[0 * 4 + 0] = mark
px[3 * 4 + 2] = mark
val c = find_centroid(px, 4, 4, mark)
assert_equal(c[0], 1)
assert_equal(c[1], 1)
assert_equal(c[2], 2)
```

</details>

#### no matching pixel returns the [-1, -1, 0] sentinel

- Verify: no matching pixel returns the [-1, -1, 0] sentinel


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: no matching pixel returns the [-1, -1, 0] sentinel")
val bg: u32 = 0xFF000000
var px: [u32] = [bg; 16]
val c = find_centroid(px, 4, 4, 0xFFFFFFFF)
assert_equal(c[0], -1)
assert_equal(c[1], -1)
assert_equal(c[2], 0)
```

</details>

### game2d.render.evidence — diff_count

#### counts the exact number of differing pixels

- Verify: counts the exact number of differing pixels


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: counts the exact number of differing pixels")
var a: [u32] = [0; 16]
var b: [u32] = [0; 16]
b[0] = 1
b[5] = 1
b[15] = 1
assert_equal(diff_count(a, b, 16), 3)
```

</details>

